The number of triangles in the given figure is shown below:

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/334c8c543b34a6fb67ff6907372e6e725f47c01966e0c3de31540623dfc077c5.png] 

Thus, there are a total of 27 triangles.

Hence, **"Option 1"** is the correct answer.

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/c76c13ba2d2ab46b47f8a931ae621dac081a0cb266b142dc23f58659fac4a466.png] **__Alternate Method__**

1) Number of triangles = {n(n + 2)(2n + 1)over 8} , Where; n = 4 (number of triangles at the baseline)

= {4(4 + 2)(2 times 4 + 1)over 8}

= {4(6)(8 + 1)over 8}

= {4 times 6 times 9over 8}

= 27
